# Postman sync

When routes, request/response schemas, query params, or auth on this Django API change, update the Postman collection through the **full** Postman MCP in `.cursor/mcp.json`. Do not hand-edit collections.

1. Resolve the target from `.cursor/postman.local.json` (per machine) then [docs/POSTMAN.md](../../docs/POSTMAN.md). Workspace **Perso**, collection **market-watch**; the whole collection is this repo.
2. Use `check-endpoint` for a read-only drift report.
3. Use `upsert-endpoint` to create or update matching requests (never delete orphaned ones — move them into a collection-root `Deprecated` folder).
4. If write tools are missing, the MCP is not on the `/mcp` (full) profile — stop and switch the URL to `https://mcp.postman.com/mcp` (or override in `~/.cursor/mcp.json` on this PC).
5. Body conventions: non-multipart bodies are **JSON** (raw language `json` / CLI `-d 'json:...'`), never Text; **do not** set a manual `Content-Type` header — Postman detects it. Always sync query + URI params from the Django route / serializers.
6. Docs tab: every request needs markdown with an opening summary plus (when applicable) `## Path Parameters`, `## Query Parameters`, `## Request Body`, `## Example Payload`, `## Response`, and `## Example Response`. Generate from OpenAPI via `scripts/generate_postman_docs.py` when possible.

Folder placement follows each `/` in the path; skip path-param segments. See `check-endpoint` / `upsert-endpoint`.
